steps.say:
On the Laptop, 3-5. In For the project admins, check and copy the seven public values address, endpoint, wireguard_public_key, network, ssh_host_key, ca_sha256 and homeserver, and check the eighth row SSH fingerprint. Its wireguard_public_key is the server's, not the Laptop's laptop key. For bring's Public host values (JSON), assemble these seven copied values, quoted as JSON strings, into this object; replace every placeholder with the matching row, without changing its value:

{"address":"<address>","endpoint":"<endpoint>","wireguard_public_key":"<wireguard_public_key>","network":"<network>","ssh_host_key":"<ssh_host_key>","ca_sha256":"<ca_sha256>","homeserver":"<homeserver>"}

Each row has its own Copy button; there is no Copy JSON button. Click Close after keeping this public object. Expected: (not run) all eight values match host.json, every copy works and the object contains exactly the seven named strings. Failure signs: missing/different values, empty clipboard, missing quotation marks or the SSH fingerprint copied as an extra property. Next in the panel moves on.
